 "result": "squeeze.py is an LZMA2 raw-format compressor. A header byte picks the best of five lc/lp/pb sets. It round-trips both public samples and is registered at baseline 5.50. I made no changes, so the gain is +0%. A context-mixing compressor in pure Python would likely beat it. I judged it too slow for the 30 s limit on inputs of about 700 KB, so I did not try it.",
